  <h2>What happened to µTorrent on the Mac</h2>
  <p>µTorrent's Mac app, now called µTorrent Classic, was a 32-bit app. With macOS Catalina in 2019, Macs stopped running 32-bit apps, and rather than rebuild it, µTorrent <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%CE%9CTorrent">moved Mac users to µTorrent Web</a>. Its last version came out in January 2020.</p>
  <p>µTorrent's <a href="https://www.utorrent.com/downloads/mac/">Mac download page</a> still offers Classic, marked “Not compatible with MAC OS Catalina Version 10.15 and above”. So on any recent Mac, µTorrent's desktop app won't open.</p>

  <h2>µTorrent Web</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.utorrent.com/web/mac/">µTorrent Web</a> runs inside your web browser: you add torrents and watch them in a browser tab, and it can play a video or a song while it downloads. The free version shows ads, and yearly subscriptions remove them. Its source code isn't public.</p>

  <h2>A Mac app instead</h2>
  <p>If you miss having a real app, OrbTorrent is one:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Free, with no ads,</strong> no account and nothing to buy. It's open source, under the GPL.</li>
    <li><strong>In your menu bar.</strong> An orb shows how your downloads are doing, and a click shows speeds, downloads and their files.</li>
    <li><strong>qBittorrent's engine</strong> does the downloading. It's free and open source too.</li>
    <li><strong>Downloads only through your VPN,</strong> if you like. If the VPN drops, downloading stops instead of carrying on without it.</li>
    <li><strong>Fake downloads held</strong> before they arrive, such as a “film” that's really a program.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>OrbTorrent needs macOS 26 or later. On an older Mac, <a href="https://transmissionbt.com">Transmission</a> runs on macOS 11 and later, and is free and open source too.</p>

  <h2>Bringing your downloads over</h2>
  <p>OrbTorrent <a href="/switch">imports downloads</a> from Transmission and qBittorrent, but not from µTorrent. To carry on with a download, open its magnet link or .torrent file in OrbTorrent and choose the folder µTorrent saved it in. OrbTorrent checks the files already there, and downloads only what's missing.</p>

  <Fragment slot="switch-title">A real app, <span class="tone">and no ads.</span></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="switch">
    <p>Download OrbTorrent and make it your Mac's torrent app when it asks. From then on, magnet links in your browser and .torrent files in Finder open in it.</p>
  </Fragment>
